#. Tag: entry
#: editor-color.docbook:922
#, no-c-format
msgid "Lens Filter Type"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: editor-color.docbook:930
#, no-c-format
msgid "Original color image taken in New Zealand landscapes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: editor-color.docbook:940
#, no-c-format
msgid "Neutral: simulate black &amp; white neutral film exposure."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: editor-color.docbook:950
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Green Filter: simulates black &amp; white film exposure with green lens "
"filter. This comes good with all scenic images, especially suited for "
"portraits taken against the sky (similar to 004 Cokin(tm) Green filter)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: editor-color.docbook:960
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Orange Filter: simulates black &amp; white film exposure with an orange lens "
"filter. This will enhance landscapes, marine scenes and aerial photography "
"(similar to 002 Cokin(tm) Orange filter)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: editor-color.docbook:970
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Red Filter: simulates black &amp; white film exposure with red lens filter. "
"Creates dramatic sky effects and can simulate moonlight scenes in daytime "
"(similar to 003 Cokin(tm) Red filter)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: editor-color.docbook:980
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Yellow Filter: simulates black &amp; white film exposure with yellow lens "
"filter. Most natural tonal correction, improves contrast. Ideal for "
"landscapes (similar to 001 Cokin(tm) Yellow filter)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: editor-color.docbook:992
#, no-c-format
msgid "Color Tint"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: editor-color.docbook:1001
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sepia Tone: gives a warm highlight and mid-tone while adding a bit of "
"coolness to the shadows - very similar to the process of bleaching a print "
"and re-developing in a sepia toner (typical for your grandmothers "
"photographs). Similar to 005 Cokin(tm) Sepia filter."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: editor-color.docbook:1011
#, no-c-format
msgid "Brown Tone: similar to Sepia Tone filter, but less pronounced."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: editor-color.docbook:1021
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Cold Tone: start subtle and replicate printing on a cold tone black &amp; "
"white paper such as a bromide enlarging paper."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: editor-color.docbook:1031
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Platinum Tone: effect that replicates traditional platinum chemical toning "
"done in the darkroom."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: editor-color.docbook:1041
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Selenium Tone: effect that replicates traditional selenium chemical toning "
"done in the darkroom."
msgstr ""
